# PR Review Correction Loop (Pre-Merge)

Merge to `main` only when **blocking CI is green** and **automated review feedback has reached quiescence** (no new actionable bot comments on the latest pushed commit).

Complements `@.cursor/rules/011-coderabbit-pr-gate.mdc` (scope) and `@.cursor/rules/012-dependabot-pr-gate.mdc` (Dependabot).

## Bots in scope (address every actionable item)

| Source | Notes |
|--------|--------|
| **CodeRabbit** (`coderabbitai`) | Inline threads + **review body** (out-of-diff findings often appear only in the summary). A check that only says **“Review rate limited”** is **not** quiescence — parse **Next review available in: N minutes**, wait `N+buffer`, then post `@coderabbitai review` and repeat until a real review targets the latest head. **After 3 cycles / >90m total**, CodeRabbit becomes optional (standing policy, not per-PR permission) as long as Sourcery has a real non-rate-limited review on the current head with everything resolved — see `011`. |
| **CodeAnt** (`codeant-ai`) | Inline suggestions + quality-gate status contexts |
| **Sourcery** (`sourcery-ai`) | Comment `@sourcery-ai review` to trigger/re-trigger on the latest head — do this whenever the latest review predates the current head commit. Inline `suggestion` / `nitpick` / `suggestion (bug_risk)` threads; `bug_risk` findings are correctness bugs and get fixed, not just acknowledged. |
| **Copilot** (`copilot-pull-request-reviewer`) | Inline PR review comments |
| **DeepSource** (`deepsource-io`) | **Mandatory:** post `@deepsourcebot review` on every PR (open + after fix pushes). Team AI Review is on-demand; without that mention only static analysis runs. Address AI Review + actionable Docker/Shell findings. Dashboard JS analyzer remains off (no `javascript` block in `.deepsource.toml`) — see `docs/deepsource-javascript-ci.md`. ESLint + `deploy.yml` are authoritative for TS/TSX. |
| **Socket Security** | Actionable PR alerts when they block merge |
| **Cursor Bugbot** | When explicitly requested |
| **Greptile / Codex** | Skip when trial or usage limits return no review (document in PR disposition comment) |

Human review comments requesting concrete fixes are in scope while open.

## Merge gate order (strict)

1. **Push** fix commits to the PR branch.
2. **Trigger** `@deepsourcebot review` (required on open and after **every** fix push to the latest head), `@coderabbitai review` whenever the latest head lacks a real CodeRabbit review (missing, stale SHA, or rate-limited placeholder), and `@sourcery-ai review` whenever the latest head lacks a Sourcery review.
3. **Wait** for blocking CI on the latest commit (`deploy.yml` Typecheck/Lint/Tests, build, security audit, Chromium + cross-browser E2E — read job logs, not badge alone for advisory jobs).
4. **Collect** all open review threads (GraphQL `reviewThreads`) and scan latest bot **review bodies** for new actionable items (include DeepSource AI Review + CodeRabbit summary). **CodeRabbit "outside diff range" findings never appear as GraphQL `reviewThreads`** — GitHub can't anchor a comment outside the diff hunk to a normal thread, so CodeRabbit folds them into the review's top-level `body` text under a collapsible "⚠️ Outside diff range comments" section instead. Fetch full review bodies via `gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/pulls/N/reviews --paginate` and grep for `outside diff` (case-insensitive) on **every** pass, not just once — a thread-only sweep will silently miss these.
5. **Fix or reply** on every thread; **resolve** threads after fix or documented rationale.
6. **Re-check** after bots finish on the new commit. For CodeRabbit rate limits: parse the wait time, sleep through it (+buffer), re-trigger `@coderabbitai review` (bounded loop in `011` — max 3 cycles / >90m waits). After that threshold, CodeRabbit is optional rather than a merge block **provided** Sourcery has a real (non-rate-limited) review on the current head with all actionable items resolved and no other in-scope bot has an unresolved item or active `CHANGES_REQUESTED` — this is standing policy (`011` step 6), not something to re-confirm per PR. **Do not merge** while CodeRabbit `CHANGES_REQUESTED` targets the **latest** head (unless the optional-CodeRabbit condition applies), while DeepSource AI Review was never attempted on the latest head, or while unresolved inline threads remain. A `CHANGES_REQUESTED` review on a **superseded** commit is not a merge block once a newer real review (or APPROVED/COMMENTED replacement) exists for the current head — dismiss or ignore the stale review state and resolve any remaining open threads.
7. **Merge** only when step 3 is green and step 6 shows no new actionable items.

Do **not** merge on stale bot approval from an older commit while newer commits are untested or unreviewed.

Do **not** use `git commit --no-verify` / `git push --no-verify` to skip Husky — pre-commit runs `typecheck`; pre-push runs `check:fast`. Bypassing hooks lets TypeScript errors reach CI after push.

## Correction loop (per finding)

1. Verify against **current** code on the PR branch (bots often comment on superseded commits).
2. **Fix** if valid; prefer minimal, focused diffs.
3. **Defer** only with a short English reply on the thread (rare — security/correctness findings should be fixed).
4. **Reply** on the inline thread citing the fixing commit when applicable.
5. **Resolve** the review thread (GitHub “Resolve conversation”).
6. Post a **PR disposition comment** when closing a large batch (bot → action table).

## CI vs advisory checks

- **Blocking:** `deploy.yml` quality gates, Chromium E2E (`e2e.yml`), cross-browser E2E (`e2e-cross-browser.yml` — Firefox/WebKit/mobile Chrome), required branch protections, Socket when flagged blocking.
- **Advisory (default):** DeepSource JavaScript (`deepsourceJavaScriptAdvisory: true`), Claude Code skipped jobs on PRs without `@claude`.
- **Claude Code `action_required`:** Workflow triggered by `pull_request_review_comment` may show **Approve and run workflows** with zero jobs — GitHub workflow-approval gate, not a failed test. Job `if` still requires `@claude` in the comment body; approval alone does not run Claude on bot threads.

## Collection commands (agents / maintainers)

```bash
# Unresolved threads with author
gh api graphql -f query='query { repository(owner:"qnbs", name:"AI-Research-Orchestrator") { pullRequest(number:N) { reviewThreads(first:100) { nodes { id isResolved comments(last:1) { nodes { databaseId author { login } body } } } } } } }'

# Latest CodeRabbit review commit
gh api repos/qnbs/AI-Research-Orchestrator/pulls/N/reviews --jq '[.[]|select(.user.login=="coderabbitai[bot]")]|sort_by(.submitted_at)|.[-1]'
```

Replace `N` with the PR number. After fixes, resolve threads via GraphQL `resolveReviewThread` or the GitHub UI.

## Lessons (standing)

- **Align identifiers end-to-end:** UI label, external URL, export/PDF, and corpus keys must use the same resolved identifier (P1-5 lesson).
- **Canonical legacy keys win:** When `pmid` and `articleId` disagree, trust the canonical `pmid` string for maps and hydration.
- **Hydrate before validation:** Run `ensureGroundedClaim` / `ensureArticleIdentifiers` before corpus validation and Dexie upgrades; guard non-string legacy keys.
- **i18n for all identifier types:** Copy toast and ARIA labels must not hard-code “PMID” when DOI/arXiv/PMCID are copied.
- **DOI URLs:** Use `encodeURI` for `doi.org` paths (preserve `/`); do not `encodeURIComponent` the full DOI.
- **CodeRabbit re-reviews** each push — expect 2–4 correction rounds on medium PRs. Rate-limit placeholders must be waited out and re-triggered (`@coderabbitai review`); never treat “Review rate limited” as approval.
- **Outside-diff-range findings hide from thread sweeps.** A GraphQL `reviewThreads` query that returns 0 unresolved can still be hiding a real finding sitting in a review's raw `body` text (CodeRabbit "⚠️ Outside diff range comments"). Confirmed in practice on PR #220: a test-quality finding (missing service-worker-controller assertion before an offline check) was caught only by grepping review bodies directly, after a thread-only pass reported clean. Always run both checks.
- **Heavy same-PR bot activity can rate-limit reviews on other PRs.** CodeRabbit's fair-usage limits appear to be repo/org-wide, not strictly per-PR — several rapid re-review cycles on one PR can leave a concurrently open PR stuck on "Review rate limited" even after its own re-trigger. If two PRs are being landed together, expect this and budget the wait accordingly rather than assuming the second PR's rate limit is a fresh, independent cooldown.
- **DeepSource noise:** JavaScript analyzer is off in the DeepSource dashboard; `.deepsource.toml` has no `javascript` block (`docs/deepsource-dashboard-off.md`). Do not churn code solely for advisory DeepSource JavaScript unless policy flips to blocking.

